# Optional. Nothing here is required: Mock needs no setup, and this app has no per-app .env.
# The shared settings file is ~/Development/.env (mode 600; STANDALONE_ENV overrides the path), read by every standalone app.
# Live reads four keys from it, as defaults, and never writes the file (values saved on the Settings page win):
# PINGONE_ENVIRONMENT_ID=         # your PingOne environment UUID
# PINGONE_REGION=                 # com, eu, ca, asia, com.au or sg
# PINGONE_CLIENT_ID=              # the PingOne worker application's client ID
# PINGONE_CLIENT_SECRET=          # its secret (write-only here). Admin credentials and vault passwords never go in that file.
#
# Per-run settings (set in the shell; the shared file holds no PORT):
# PORT=4840                       # must be in 4840-4849 (Vite dev server: VITE_PORT, default 4841)
# P1AZ_BIND=                      # loopback only unless you set this on purpose (the container does)
# P1AZ_ALLOWED_HOSTS=             # extra Host names to accept when P1AZ_BIND is set (comma-separated)
# DATA_DIR=                       # this app's own settings folder (default ~/.p1az-inspector, mode 700)
